title: Munich Holds Out
subtitle: The strikes in the north have bought the council republic a week.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_bavaria = 1 and crisis_time >= 4 and e19_bav_ring = 1 and e19_bav_whites > 7
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_whites -= 7;
Q.e19_bav_food -= 7;
if (Q.e19_bav_food < 0) { Q.e19_bav_food = 0; Q.e19_bav_hungry = 1; Q.e19_bav_army = Math.max(1, Q.e19_bav_army - 4); }
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Von Oven\'s army: ' + Q.e19_bav_whites + ' days from Munich';
Q.crisis_line_2 = Q.e19_bav_food > 0 ? 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days' : 'Food in Munich: none';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e19_bav_army + ',000 men';
!}

= Munich Holds Out

Von Oven has had to leave regiments in Saxony and the Ruhr, and his attack is put off by a week. In Munich the milk is gone, and the queues outside the bakeries start before dawn.

- @cellars: Open the cellars of the hotels and the villas.
- @peasants: Pay the peasants of the Dachau moor in Reich marks.

@cellars
subtitle: Food for a week. The middle class will welcome the Whites as liberators.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_food += 7;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 1;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days';
!}

The cellars of the Bayerischer Hof give up hams and flour. The working-class districts eat for a week.

@peasants
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Less food, and the villages will not shoot at the Red Army.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no money to send.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e19_bav_food += 4;
Q.bav_peasants += 1;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days';
!}

Carts roll in from the moor with milk and potatoes, paid for in real money.
